    "captions": {
      "video": "qbw-vid-002",
      "segments": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "duration": 6.2,
          "text": "Your old disc brake pads are worn and you can hear it every time you stop."
        },
        {
          "start": 6.2,
          "duration": 6.2,
          "text": "Today I'll show you how to replace disc brake pads in about ten minutes at home."
        },
        {
          "start": 12.4,
          "duration": 5.8,
          "text": "We do this job on a lot of bikes every week here at the shop."
        },
        {
          "start": 18.2,
          "duration": 6.5,
          "text": "It's easier than it looks, and you only need a few basic tools to get it done."
        },
        {
          "start": 24.7,
          "duration": 6.9,
          "text": "And by the end your brakes will feel sharp and quiet again, like the day you bought them."
        },
        {
          "start": 31.6,
          "duration": 6.9,
          "text": "Before we start, if you're new here, hit subscribe and the bell, it really helps the channel grow."
        },
        {
          "start": 38.5,
          "duration": 1.9,
          "text": "Okay, let's get into it."
        },
        {
          "start": 40.4,
          "duration": 6.2,
          "text": "Here's what you need: a hex key set, a flat screwdriver, a clean rag, isopropyl alcohol,"
        },
        {
          "start": 46.6,
          "duration": 6.5,
          "text": "a pad spreader or an old tyre lever, a torque wrench, new pads that match your caliper,"
        },
        {
          "start": 53.1,
          "duration": 5.8,
          "text": "and some gloves, because you never want skin oil on the pads or the rotor."
        },
        {
          "start": 58.9,
          "duration": 6.5,
          "text": "But first, a quick word from today's sponsor, Brindlecog Tools, who make the torque wrench I use."
        },
        {
          "start": 65.4,
          "duration": 6.9,
          "text": "Brindlecog has been making workshop tools for years and their wrenches are some of the most accurate around."
        },
        {
          "start": 72.3,
          "duration": 8.1,
          "text": "The one I'm using covers the range you need for brakes, stems and bars, and it clicks at the set torque."
        },
        {
          "start": 80.4,
          "duration": 6.9,
          "text": "It comes in a hard case with every bit you need, and it is calibrated before it ships."
        },
        {
          "start": 87.3,
          "duration": 6.9,
          "text": "I've used mine for two seasons in the shop and it still reads true when we check it."
        },
        {
          "start": 94.2,
          "duration": 6.5,
          "text": "Use the code in the description for a discount, and thanks to Brindlecog for supporting the channel."
        }
      ]
    },
